<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Ahtum</h1><p class="st-meta">990 CE – 1028 CE (approx.) · capital Morisena</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Realm in the Banat ruled from Morisena by Ahtum (Ajtony), a powerful Orthodox lord defeated by Stephen I of Hungary.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahtum">Ahtum</a> is known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legend-of-saint-gerard">Legend of Saint Gerard</a>. Around 1000 he held the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mures-river">Mureș</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenad">Morisena</a> (Cenad). He had been baptised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> rite at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a> makes him a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glad">Glad</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-glad">Duchy of Glad</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahtum">Ahtum</a> was rich in horses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and taxed the salt carried down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mures-river">Mureș</a> to the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, which provoked conflict. He founded a Greek monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenad">Morisena</a>, staffed by Byzantine monks, and recognised Byzantine authority.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Stephen I sent his commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/csanad-commander">Csanád</a>, who defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahtum">Ahtum</a>. Historians date this either to around 1003 or to around 1028. Csanád became count of the region, renamed Csanád, and Gerard founded a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> bishopric there, part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1000-1301">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1000-1301).</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-ahtum.jpg" alt="Duchy of Ahtum" width="320" height="187"><figcaption>Image: GeorgeBasaraba · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banatul_Timi%C8%99oarei_.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>990 CE – 1028 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Morisena</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahtum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ajtony's realm, Realm of Ahtum</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1009&amp;focus=duchy-of-ahtum" aria-label="Duchy of Ahtum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5277 573 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Ahtum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5446 783h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5597 829h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5597 829h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=1009&amp;focus=duchy-of-ahtum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

